// Maturity review notes, CSUEB 2025-2026 Instructional Materials, 2026-10-23.
// One Note per indicator, attached with has_note, created_by Daniel Fontaine.
// include_in_report=false: internal review notes, kept out of the public report.
// Idempotent: MERGE on note name; re-run refreshes content.

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-1.1-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-1.1-ins-csueb-a75f9b11'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The formal instruments exist: Academic Affairs Directive 2018-01 and 24-25 CIC 47, recorded together with the policy PDF linked. The campus does not yet have a standard practice. Pamela Baird (2026-08-19) calls faculty compliance with timely adoption a real problem, and Zach Oshri\'s department survey found adoption practice varies widely and is documented nowhere. The adoption rate runs at 45 to 55 percent. The CSUEB Textbook Adoption Monitoring Platform is still in test at about 80 percent link accuracy. Ownership is shared between Kristin Hart and Zach Oshri with no single owner. CIC 47 has no recorded approval or effective date. A policy on paper is not a standard practice (principle:capability-maturity-over-binary-compliance).\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Get the reissued adoption policy out from the current provost\'s office, and record when CIC 47 was approved and when it took effect.\n2. Name one owner for timely adoption and write the duty into that position description.\n3. Move the adoption monitoring platform out of test and start the faculty reminders, so each term\'s adoption rate is on record.\n\nOwned by another area: The bookstore and Follett run adoption collection (Joyce Bold is the working contact). No boundary is stated for that reliance.\n\nRecord problems: The retired item Policy on Timely Adoption is still listed and shares its PDF with the CIC 47 item. The Affordable Learning Committee item has no strength rating and no owner. The CIC 47 item has no owner, and its page title is misspelled (4-25 CIC 47 ... Acessibility). The reminder email cites 25-26 CIC 46 and CIC 2006-07, and neither is listed.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-1.2-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-1.2-ins-csueb-66b64d36'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: high.\n\nBasis: Two items are listed: Textbook Adoption Internal Tracking (department contacts) and the adoption monitoring platform. The deadline reminders (newsletter announcements, Canvas pop-ups, bookstore emails) exist only as March 2026 notes. The bar asks for an enforced campuswide process that adopts on behalf of late-assigned instructors; the survey names late assignment as the root cause, and nothing addresses it. No training and no periodic review are recorded, and the provost\'s messaging strategy is still in development. The monitoring platform meets the tracking requirement, with the caveat that it is in test (53 percent adoption rate reported three weeks before term). Nothing shows staff time allocated to adoption coordination.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Write the campuswide adoption procedure, including what happens when an instructor is assigned late, and list the reminder steps the bookstore and Online Campus already run.\n2. Show in a position description or budget line who coordinates adoption and how much time it gets.\n3. Run a recurring faculty session on adoption deadlines and accessible materials, and review the process once a year.\n\nOwned by another area: Same bookstore and Follett reliance as 1.1.\n\nRecord problems: The reminder practice exists only as notes. Course Accessibility & Timeline (Accessibility Services) publishes the deadlines but is listed only under 4.1 and 4.5. The Textbook_Adoption_Form_Simplified document has never had its content saved.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-1.6-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-1.6-ins-csueb-8fb8ec10'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: high.\n\nBasis: The only item is the adoption monitoring platform, with no strength rating here. The July 2026 note says its dashboard positions it to produce semester reports once it leaves test, which is intent. Nothing shows a report delivered to campus administration, a schedule, or a named distributor. The March 2026 note about the Dean of Libraries tracking late-hire faculty is also intent. All five bar requirements are unmet.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. Send one adoption performance report from the platform dashboard to the provost\'s office this term, and record who received it.\n2. Write down the schedule and the person responsible for compiling and distributing the report each semester.\n\nRecord problems: The platform link has no strength rating.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-4.1-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-4.1-ins-csueb-e6e070fe'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Guidance and training are strong. ScreenSteps Faculty Guides (Canvas & Accessibility) holds 53 Canvas guides with saved content, and Annual Back to the Bay Workshops runs an Accessibility in your Canvas Course session with a sign-in sheet. CIC 47 states the accessibility expectation. Nothing shows LMS use is widespread across units, because no usage counts exist, and nothing shows the process is reviewed. The three Senate policies that would make posting formal (21-22 CIC 44 LMS Opening Timeline, 22-23 CIC 6 Syllabus Policy Update, 23-24 CIC 1 Canvas for waitlisted students) carry no description, and CIC 44 and CIC 1 have no link. The syllabus must be posted by day one, but East Bay has no central syllabus repository, so compliance cannot be seen.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Describe and link CIC 44, the Syllabus Policy Update and the waitlist policy, and record CIC 47\'s approval date, so the posting requirement can be read on the record.\n2. Collect Canvas usage counts by college each term.\n3. Review the guides and workshop each year against that usage, and record the review.\n\nRecord problems: CIC 44 and CIC 1 have empty descriptions, no strength rating and no link. CIC 6 has an empty description. Two Back to the Bay documents have never had their content saved.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-4.11-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-4.11-ins-csueb-2c0ca57b'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The LTI Accessibility Review and Approval Gate is a real hard gate, but it covers tools entering Canvas, not faculty-maintained sites. About ICT Purchases - VPAT covers purchases, has no owner and is rated weak. Two notes contradict each other: the March 2026 note says no process is in place, and an undated note says faculty sites generally follow the ICT review. No reviews, records, discovery method or faculty guidance are recorded. All six bar requirements are unmet.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. Write a short procedure for how a faculty-maintained site or app is reviewed, including sites hosted off campus, and how such sites are found.\n2. Keep a record of each review and what was fixed.\n3. Publish faculty guidance that names the route.\n\nOwned by another area: Review of purchased products belongs to procurement. The open question for this indicator is whether a faculty site has any route into that review.\n\nRecord problems: The two notes contradict each other; settle it with Zach Oshri. About ICT Purchases - VPAT has no owner.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-4.5-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-4.5-ins-csueb-d9ec4823'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Alt Media Request & Fulfillment Automation, operated by Zach Oshri, gives production staff the adopted-title list ahead of term from the Follett feed. Accessible Media Production (Accessibility Services) publishes term-based intake. That covers early access to textbook data, and its value depends on adoption compliance, which is weak (see 1.1). The indicator asks for access to materials inside the LMS. The 2026-08-18 note says there are no documented Canvas roles or permissions for alt media staff and no record of access granted before instruction. The March 2026 note describes reactive outreach.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Define and document the Canvas role alt media staff hold and when they are added to courses each term.\n2. Keep a per-term record of when access was granted against the start of instruction.\n3. Add one line to faculty guidance asking instructors to post materials early, and say who grants access.\n\nOwned by another area: Intake belongs to Accessibility Services and production to Zach Oshri\'s unit. The boundary between them is not stated.\n\nRecord problems: Sources disagree on ownership: Zach\'s note puts production in ITS, and Pamela Baird says it moved to Online Campus. The retired directive is still listed. Three of the automation\'s four pages have never had their content saved.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.11-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.11-ins-csueb-35efa53e'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Automated Verbit Captioning Activation (CSUEB Online Campus) is a documented, owned process that turns on captioning for every new Canvas and Panopto shell each night. Accessibility Compliance for Digital Teaching & Learning states the faculty captioning obligation and a dated rollout timeline. Remediation is informal: the only remediation service (Accessible Remediation, Accessibility Services) is retired, and the remaining note says faculty and staff can submit a service ticket. Nothing records selection criteria for media tools, a vendor contract, or monitoring data. Turning captioning on is not proof that captions exist by the first class meeting.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Write down the media remediation path: who takes a request, the turnaround, and who pays for captioning and audio description, with the Verbit agreement on file.\n2. Keep a record each term of captioned or remediated media for active courses, checked against the start of instruction.\n3. Save the content of the captioning automation\'s documentation page, and add guidance on choosing accessible media tools.\n\nRecord problems: The Verbit documentation page has no saved content. The compliance page\'s description gives the deadline as April 24, 2026; the live page says April 24, 2027.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.12-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.12-ins-csueb-dba4e9f5'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: low.\n\nBasis: The only listed item is the general guidance page Accessibility Compliance for Digital Teaching & Learning, which never names course readers and has no strength rating. The CSUEB Instructional Materials page tells faculty to plan ahead and contact Online Campus or Accessibility Services about remediation. Two notes describe the routes: the Online Campus eLearning Specialist, and Library e-reserves and OER services. The routes are consistent but informal. Defined rests mostly on notes; any further loss of evidence drops it to Initiated.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Describe the course reader process in one place: how a reader is built accessibly, who checks it, and how remediation is requested.\n2. List the Library e-reserves and OER service as evidence, with a named owner.\n3. Record who does reader remediation and how it is funded.\n\nRecord problems: The guidance link has no strength rating. The Library service exists only in a note.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.13-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.13-ins-csueb-dce52475'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Two items carry the grade: the Equalify Reflow PDF Accessibility Pipeline, with an owner and documentation, and the guidance page, which links the AY 2025-26 course materials checklist, UDOIT and TidyUP workshops, and Microsoft 365 and Adobe instructions. Notes say 14 student assistants work with the eLearning Specialist on remediation at about $70,000 to $80,000 a year. That is the strongest resource fact, but it is not listed as an item and no allocation record backs it. Reflow is still in testing on borrowed GPU capacity. The 2024-2025 note says there is no formal process, and procedures remain informal.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Make the document remediation workflow formal (intake, triage, student assistant work, faculty sign-off) and publish it where faculty already go.\n2. List the student assistant remediation service as evidence, with its funding and the eLearning Specialist\'s role recorded.\n3. Save the Reflow documentation page and state whether the pipeline is in production or a pilot.\n\nOwned by another area: Review of third-party content before purchase belongs to procurement. Hosting for Reflow is an open question to SFBRN.\n\nRecord problems: The guidance and Reflow links have no strength rating. The Reflow page has no saved content. Two 2024-2025 notes are identical. The 2026 versus 2027 deadline contradiction applies here too.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.14-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.14-ins-csueb-33a57113'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The LTI Accessibility Review and Approval Gate (CSUEB Online Campus) is a real hard gate; its worked-examples note records at least twelve integrations denied in 2025-26. It covers Canvas integrations only, which meets the review-before-use requirement for that slice. AI and other emerging tools outside Canvas rely on the ITC AI guidelines draft, still awaiting Provost approval, and a planned faculty checklist; both are plans. Nothing records risks, alternate activities or equivalent outcomes when a tool falls short.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. Extend the review beyond Canvas integrations to AI and other emerging tools, and finish approval of the AI guidelines.\n2. Write the procedure for when a tool cannot be made fully accessible: record the risk and build an alternate activity with an equivalent outcome.\n3. Publish the faculty selection checklist and list the existing guidance page as evidence here.\n\nOwned by another area: Vendor conformance report review belongs to procurement. The gate is the hand-off and is what is graded here.\n\nRecord problems: The gate has no strength rating, no stated boundary here (it is marked internal on 4.11), and no linked page or document. Dan Legate is listed with no role.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.15-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.15-ins-csueb-7e5e978c'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The LTI gate reviews publisher platforms that enter Canvas (for example the Expert TA conformance report review) and records each review as an ICT questionnaire in P2P. That meets the selection review and documentation tracking requirements for Canvas-delivered content. A note confirms publisher content in the LMS must clear the ICT review. Publisher content outside Canvas has no recorded process: about 125 Follett Inclusive Access sections, plus textbooks. The Dean of Libraries tracking process is an intention only. Proactive remediation and faculty support are not recorded here.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Extend review to Inclusive Access and textbook adoptions, with a tracking record for each title.\n2. Write a step for arranging remediation or alternate formats before the term when publisher content falls short, tied to adoption deadlines.\n3. List the faculty guidance on choosing publisher materials as evidence here.\n\nOwned by another area: Conformance report review quality belongs to procurement. Follett tracking belongs to the Library and Bookstore.\n\nRecord problems: No boundary stated on the gate link.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-5.16-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-5.16-ins-csueb-bb033b73'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The LTI gate is the campus\'s consistent selection and adoption control, with a named owner, a procurement participant, and records of twelve or more denials. The older VPAT Process is retired. Established needs formal, communicated documentation and allocated resources. The gate has no linked procedure document, and only Zach Oshri\'s position description is on record. Creating tools and remediating them after adoption are not covered.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Publish the gate procedure (request, conformance report review, questionnaire, P2P, decision) and link it from faculty guidance.\n2. Add a step for tools already in use: periodic re-review and remediation or replacement.\n3. Record whose position descriptions include the review: the Online Campus lead and the Business Operations Specialist.\n\nOwned by another area: Vendor conformance review belongs to procurement; the gate is the instructional unit\'s hand-off.\n\nRecord problems: No boundary stated on the gate link. The retired VPAT Process has no description.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.2-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-6.2-ins-csueb-6d7c8976'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The scope is selecting, authoring and procuring. Procuring has one practice, the LTI Accessibility Review and Approval Gate, which is a hard stop for Canvas integrations but is undocumented and covers learning tools only. Selecting rests on one note (remediate or offer an OER alternative). Nothing covers authoring. SFBRN TAAP Authoring Process concerns procurement exceptions and is peripheral here. CIC 47 requires accessibility verification at the adoption deadline and is close to the procedures requirement, but it is not listed here. All four bar requirements are unmet.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. List CIC 47 and the textbook adoption directive as the selection procedure, and write down the review steps the Online Campus already runs.\n2. Name the authoring support faculty use, such as guides or consultation, and list it here.\n3. Keep a record of materials checked at adoption, so launch-ready courses can be counted.\n\nOwned by another area: Conformance review of vendor tools belongs to procurement. The gate is the campus interface to it.\n\nRecord problems: SFBRN TAAP Authoring Process has no stated boundary, and its page is a Qualtrics editor link readers cannot open. The gate\'s owner shows as the role placeholder ATI Coordinator.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.4-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-6.4-ins-csueb-6bb4c3c0'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The one item is the Accessible Course Materials Remediation Form, an opt-in faculty request service with no strength rating and no saved page content. A request form gives faculty a route to remediation. It is not a required review before posting, so the before-posting scope is unmet. CIC 47 and Course Accessibility & Timeline (Accessibility Services) both state pre-term deadlines, but neither is listed here. Zach Oshri\'s role is in his position description; the bar asks for assignment across relevant roles.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. Write down a review step that course materials pass before a revised course is published, and list CIC 47 and the Accessibility Services timeline as its basis.\n2. Keep a log of revised courses reviewed and remediated each term.\n3. Record who besides the Accessibility Specialist carries review work.\n\nRecord problems: Neither form page has saved content. The two form links appear to point at the same form.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.5-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-6.5-ins-csueb-d8e32011'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Two items are listed: 24-25 CIC 47/FAC 14/FDEC 5, with no owner and no strength rating, and the Instructional Materials - ATI guidance pages listing faculty responsibilities each term. Neither describes a redesign process with accessibility at its stages. The only redesign evidence is a note saying accessibility is covered if the faculty member is in the Quality Assurance/Quality Matters program, with tutorials for everyone else. That is a common practice for a subset of faculty. CIC 47 shows CIC (2/17/25) and FAC (3/5/25) votes but no Senate approval or effective date.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Describe the Quality Assurance/Quality Matters redesign process and its accessibility checkpoints, list it here, and add the path for faculty outside the program.\n2. Name the instructional designers who support redesign and show that their position descriptions include this work.\n3. Record the CIC 47 Senate approval and effective date, and collect accessibility results before and after redesign.\n\nRecord problems: CIC 47 has no owner and its page title is misspelled. The QA/QM program appears only in a note.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.7-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-6.7-ins-csueb-4006a0d0'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: The automated half is strong. The Instructional Materials Remediation Dashboard pulls UDOIT reports nightly and builds a department scorecard that drives direct outreach, which meets the output requirement. UDOIT Course Accessibility Scanning & Bulk Remediation (UDOITOrchestrator) has public process documentation. No manual evaluation method or schedule is recorded, so half the scope is silent. Both items depend on one person, Zach Oshri. The leaderboard plan is intent.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Write down the evaluation schedule and the manual checks (for example keyboard, document and media review) that accompany the UDOIT scans.\n2. Document which staff and funds keep the scanning and dashboard running beyond one person.\n3. Save a copy of the dashboard\'s content or a periodic export, so results can be read without the live Power BI link.\n\nRecord problems: The dashboard page has no saved content and the link has no strength rating.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.8-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-6.8-ins-csueb-f9505cef'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Remediation runs through several channels: the remediation request form, UDOITOrchestrator bulk remediation, the Equalify Reflow PDF pipeline, and the dashboard. The prioritization rule exists only in notes (based on upcoming courses each semester) and is not a documented framework of impact, risk and course context. Zach Oshri\'s August 2026 note says about 70 percent of contacted faculty never respond and the result does not amount to full compliance; a year of manual work remediated 174 courses against 2,400 to 2,600 shells per semester. Zach Oshri owns all four items.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Write the prioritization rule into a short procedure: which courses come first by enrollment, required status and barrier severity, and what happens when faculty do not respond.\n2. Record the staff and student-assistant time funded for remediation, and the roles beyond the Accessibility Specialist.\n3. Report remediation coverage each term against the number of course shells.\n\nRecord problems: The Reflow and remediation form pages have no saved content. Three of four links have no strength rating. Two identical notes from 2026-03-04 are duplicates.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-6.9-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
