ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: SFBRN CSUBuy IT Accessibility Review Procedure has a saved IT Accessibility Review Procedure v1.0 stating when a TAAP is required and how to draft, route, sign, file and reference one, and a CSUEB TAAP Blank Template exists. That meets the procedures requirement for purchases that go through procurement. The LMS and LTI scope is the gap: the note LTI is a weak spot says LTI is not called out in the TAAP process, and the LTI gate is not listed here. CSUEB Equal Access Plan EAP is retired. No records show TAAPs reaching students in time, and no roles are formally assigned.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Add the LTI review gate to the TAAP procedure, so a failing Canvas integration triggers a plan, and list the gate here.\n2. Name who initiates, approves and implements a TAAP at East Bay, and show it in the position descriptions.\n3. Keep the completed TAAP log with the dates students received alternate access.\n\nOwned by another area: TAAP authoring is run by the SFBRN Procurement team for three campuses, yet both links are marked internal. Confirm the boundary. The LTI-in-TAAP gap also belongs on the CSUEB procurement indicator 1.9.\n\nRecord problems: The SFBRN TAAP Authoring Process page is a Qualtrics editor link. The retired EAP is still linked.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-7.1-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-7.1-ins-csueb-ecb6178c'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Managed. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Managed needs tracking procedures and collected measures; there are none, and no notes or owners. 24-25 CIC 47/FAC 14/FDEC 5 states faculty responsibility plainly (Faculty are responsible for creating materials that meet the required accessibility standards), so procedures and documentation reach Established on their own. The grade holds at Defined for two reasons. No one is named as enforcing the policy, and no position description or budget is attached. The saved text is the February 2025 referral memo to the Senate, which records CIC and FAC approval but not the Senate vote or the presidential signature.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Replace the linked memo with the signed, published policy and record the approval date.\n2. Name the office that keeps the policy and checks compliance, and point to the position description or allocation that covers that work.\n3. Retire the superseded 2007-08 CIC 8 entry so only the current policy stands as evidence.\n\nRecord problems: 2007-08 CIC 8 is superseded, its page no longer exists, and it still counts as strong evidence. The CIC 47 page title is misspelled. Neither item has an owner.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-7.11-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-7.11-ins-csueb-5c6c5084'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Initiated. The evidence supports: Initiated. Confidence: high.\n\nBasis: The only item is Chancellor\'s Office Access to eResources, a systemwide repository of 508 statements for the Electronic Core Collection, run outside the campus, with no owner and no saved content. The September 2026 notes put library remediation with Zach Oshri through Accessibility Services, absorbed into his role with no allocated time or funding. They record zero requests through the barrier pathway and an unclear scope, possibly interlibrary loan only. Nothing covers converting, digitizing, creating or maintaining library assets, and nothing is written down. The two open recommendations from 2026-09-16 still describe the position.\n\nTo reach Defined:\n1. Write down the barrier routing that runs today (where a user reports, Accessibility Services triage, Zach Oshri\'s team resolves, what record is kept), and settle whether it covers all library assets.\n2. Ask the library how it checks open-access collections before enabling them in Alma, and how it handles items it digitizes or creates.\n3. Confirm whether a library position description names digital accessibility duties, and get the text.\n\nOwned by another area: Review of licensed content belongs to SFBRN procurement through CSU Buy and to the Chancellor\'s Office, which runs the Unified Library Services Platform. It does not count against the library.\n\nRecord problems: The eResources item should be marked as external, has no strength rating or owner, and links to a SharePoint list.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-7.3-ins-csueb'})
