ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Defined. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Accessibility Compliance for Digital Teaching & Learning (owners Zach Oshri and Dawna Komorosky) is a published faculty resource: the AY 2025-26 course materials checklist, ScreenSteps Canvas guides, Word, PowerPoint and PDF how-tos, a two-year readiness timeline, recurring workshops, and a recommended syllabus statement. Procedures and documentation are near Established. Resources hold the grade: no position description or budget covers the program. The common syllabus elements loaded into Canvas shells still carry no accessibility language, though Accessibility Services already publishes a statement that could go in.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Point to the position descriptions or the Online Campus and Faculty Development allocation that funds the checklist, guides and workshops.\n2. Add the Accessibility Services syllabus statement to the common syllabus elements loaded into every Canvas shell.\n3. Rate how strongly each listed item answers this indicator, with a sentence on how the checklist and workshops form the faculty process.\n\nOwned by another area: The syllabus policy belongs to the Academic Senate committee that owns it; the open recommendation already routes it.\n\nRecord problems: Strength is unset on both links.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

