MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-8.12-ins-csueb-2d506d48'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: One item is listed, Accessibility Compliance for Digital Teaching & Learning. Its four saved pages show a recurring practice: the Online Campus workshop schedule (UDOIT and TidyUP training, drop-in Canvas accessibility sessions, a compliance update) and an ADA section on the Faculty Development Resources page. Three facts hold it at Defined. Notes from 2026-08-31 say attendance is voluntary and light, with headcounts only. Orientation includes accessibility only as an invited-guest slot. The five-session Title II series is published only for AY 2024-25, and it is unconfirmed whether it ran in 2025-26. Dawna Komorosky says her role has no training budget.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Write down the process (the standing slot in new faculty and lecturer orientation, who delivers it, what it covers) and publish it where Faculty Development keeps its programs.\n2. Name the faculty development accessibility duties in the Faculty Development and Online Campus position descriptions, and record the funding behind the workshops.\n3. Confirm whether the Title II series or a successor ran in 2025-26, and if it did, list it for this year.\n\nOwned by another area: The attendance mandate belongs to the Academic Senate; the open recommendation already routes it to Benjamin Smith through Mark Robinson.\n\nRecord problems: The item\'s description gives the Title II date as April 24, 2026; the live page says 2027. No strength or boundary set. Annual Back to the Bay Workshops fits here but is listed only on 8.11, 4.1 and 4.3.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-8.13-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-8.13-ins-csueb-814c4746'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: low.\n\nBasis: The only item, Accessibility Compliance for Digital Teaching & Learning, is guidance on the legal obligation and the division of roles. It does not describe how accessibility enters academic technology work, and it has no notes or rationale. The pages show a common practice (Canvas accessibility sessions, UDOIT, a live compliance dashboard), which supports Defined at most. Stronger work exists but is not listed here: the LTI Accessibility Review and Approval Gate, UDOIT Course Accessibility Scanning & Bulk Remediation, Automated Verbit Captioning Activation and the Instructional Materials Remediation Dashboard. Listed and checked, the gate and UDOIT work could support Established. Zach Oshri\'s role is the only position evidence, and there is no budget evidence.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. List the LTI review gate, the UDOIT scanning work and the captioning activation as evidence here, each with a sentence on how it builds accessibility into academic technology work.\n2. Document the process end to end (tool request, accessibility review, Canvas deployment, ongoing scanning) and store it with the Online Campus pages.\n3. Record which positions and budget lines carry the academic technology accessibility work.\n\nOwned by another area: The vendor conformance review inside the LTI gate hands off to SFBRN procurement; only the hand-off is graded here.\n\nRecord problems: Same 2026 versus 2027 date contradiction. No strength or boundary set.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-8.14-ins-csueb'})
