MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-8.3-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
MERGE (n:Note {name: 'maturity-review-oct-2026-yse:2025-2026-8.3-ins-csueb-915f5a1f'})
ON CREATE SET n.unique_id = replace(randomUUID(), '-', ''), n.date_created = date('2026-10-23'), n.depreciated = false, n.include_in_report = false
SET n.content = 'Maturity review, 2026-10-23 (Daniel Fontaine). Recorded status: Established. The evidence supports: Defined. Confidence: medium.\n\nBasis: Remediation training is strong. ScreenSteps Faculty Guides (Canvas & Accessibility) has written guides for UDOIT, Acrobat checking, reading order and OCR, Grackle Docs, and Panopto and Verbit captioning, with saved content and named owners (Cheryl Saelee, Zach Oshri). The Online Campus workshop pages add live, Zoom, drop-in and recorded formats, so the modality side is covered. The content side is not. Creating has only course-design workshops without accessibility content. Selecting and adopting have no current material; the procurement session ran only in the AY 2024-25 Faculty Development series. Strength on one slice and silence on another is a coverage gap. No budget record exists.\n\nTo reach Established:\n1. Add training material on selecting and adopting accessible materials and tools, tied to the textbook adoption deadline and the tool review process, and keep it available after live sessions end.\n2. Write a short process for how training materials are produced, reviewed and refreshed, and who owns each set.\n3. Save the campus list of past and current trainings in the campus record.\n\nOwned by another area: Tool selection review sits with SFBRN procurement; this indicator needs only the faculty-facing training on using that process.\n\nRecord problems: ScreenSteps, the strongest item, is rated as no evidence on this link. The Google Doc training list from the 2024-2025 note has never been captured. Annual Back to the Bay Workshops is not listed here. The completed plan Incorporate CCC training resources into SFBRN ATI has no matching item.'
MERGE (y)-[:has_note]->(n)
MERGE (n)-[:created_by]->(p);

MATCH (y:YearSuccessEvidence {year_identifier: '2025-2026-9.2-ins-csueb'})
MATCH (p:Person {unique_id: 'a1d223af-c7aa-466b-bf54-47f0a199696d'})
